course: dictionary
lesson: 8419
title: One word, many meanings: rush
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word rush can mean to move very fast, a hurry, or a plant. «A girl in Dublin always left in a rush and ran across the road to catch the bus.» Here a rush is a hurry, because she was going too fast.
explain: Look at the words next to rush. «Rush hour» is the busy time when roads and trains are full. «A rush of water» means a sudden strong flow, not a hurry at all. Ask: what does rush mean in this sentence, and does my meaning still fit?
explain: Rushing is not always safe. Near pools, on stairs and across roads, rushing can cause accidents, so walk and don't run. When you read a story and a character rushes to help, the word tells you they are moving very fast because something needs doing.
fact: Rush can be a verb (to move or do something very fast) or a noun (a hurry, a sudden strong movement, or a busy time).
fact: «In a rush» means in a hurry.
fact: «Rush hour» is the busy time when roads and trains are at their fullest.
fact: «Rushes» can also be a tall, grass-like plant that grows near water.
fact: When you flush a toilet, «water rushes into the bowl», which means it moves in fast and with force.
exercise: «A girl in Dublin always left in a rush.» What does in a rush mean here? | Very cold | *In a hurry | Sad and slow | Lost on the way
exercise: «Rush hour» is when roads and trains are at their busiest. What does rush hour mean? | A quiet time at night | The hour before bed | *A busy time when roads and trains are full | A time when the shops are closed
exercise: «Heat the milk, and it suddenly rushes over the edge of the pan.» What does rushes mean here? | A tall grass growing by the water | *A sudden strong movement | A slow drip | A quiet bubble
test: «She felt a rush of joy when she saw the sea.» What does rush mean in this sentence? | A slow walk | A quiet time | *A sudden strong feeling | A tall grass by the water
test: Mum says, «Don't rush me!» What does she mean? | Please run faster | *Please don't hurry me | Please rush out of the room | Please be quiet
exam: «Rushes grow along the edge of the pond.» Which meaning fits rushes here? | A busy time on the roads | A sudden strong feeling | A hurry to get somewhere | *A tall grass-like plant that grows near water
